<title>USA: NY 1996 air cargo exports down on previous year.</title>
<headline>NY 1996 air cargo exports down on previous year.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air cargo exports from the New York customs district were some 472,509 tonnes (excluding mail) in 1996 against the slightly higher 479,197 tonnes in 1995, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey said.</p>
<p>The top ten exported commodities in tonnes and as percentage of total New York district exports and the 1995 tonnages are:</p>
<p> Commodity		    1996	As pct of   1995</p>
<p>					     '96 total</p>
<p> 1.Machinery		  86,738   18.4	 97,107</p>
<p> 2.Electrical Machinery   86,252   18.3	 70,006</p>
<p> 3.Optical Med. Inst.     31,905    6.8	 30,457</p>
<p> 4.Fish and Seafood	 19,853    4.2	 23.231</p>
<p> 5. Plastic		   17,146    3.7	 17,142</p>
<p> 6.Book, Newspaper	  16,429    3.5	 20,519</p>
<p> 7.Paper, Paperboard	15,392    3.3	 20,115</p>
<p> 8.Aircraft, Spacecraft   11,777    2.5	  8,601</p>
<p> 9.Vehicles, not Railway  10,232    2.2	 12,200</p>
<p> 10.Iron and Steel	  10,036    2.1	  7,027</p>
<p> Total NY District	 472,509		 479,197</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo New4sroom Tel+44 17144 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
